  "conclusions": [
    "Five-second warmup did not remove the approximately 40 after-paint callbacks/second plateau.",
    "Pinning only the test process to CPUs 6-7 reduced its measured CPU time substantially while the final seven seconds still had 39-40 callbacks/second. This is limited single-run evidence; no permanent affinity change is justified.",
    "The summaries preserve interval median/p95, not chronological intervals; they cannot establish strict 16.7/33.3 millisecond alternation.",
    "Application process CPU alone excludes compositor/Xorg/GPU waits and does not identify the bottleneck.",
    "Frame callbacks and GDK feedback are not a physical display rate measurement."
  ],
